# Internal research and planning drafts. Working notes, not documentation:
# each describes the codebase at the moment it was written and then goes stale
# without anything saying so. SECURITY_BRIEF.md was the case that mattered — it
# analysed v1 in the present tense ("as shipped today"), and sitting at the repo
# root it read as a statement about the shipped version long after v2 closed
# what it described.
#
# Paths are anchored with a leading slash on purpose: docs/superpowers/specs/,
# docs/v2-*.md and the 2026-07-10 plan are tracked deliberately and must not be
# caught by a broader pattern.
/RESEARCH-BRIEF*.md
/SECURITY_BRIEF.md
/research-prompt.md
/research/
/docs/ssh-hardening-brief.md
/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-08-ssh-mcp-v2.md

# Agent worktrees, created by review tooling.
.claude/worktrees/
